{%- doc -%}
  A portrait photo card with a bottom gradient, an italic heading and an
  optional short caption in the bottom-left corner, linking to an
  arbitrary href. Originally built for the homepage's "Curated for every
  occasion" row (Slow Mornings / Entertaining / Sunday Roast / High Tea);
  reused since 2026-09-14 for the homepage "Explore by category" row and
  the Cafe page's "Bring the Lambruk experience home" row, both of which
  need to link to Shop All with a tag filter pre-applied
  (`/collections/all?view=all&filter.p.tag=...`) rather than to a
  collection's own page — something `sections/collection-list.liquid`'s
  native card can't do, since its href is hardcoded to `collection.url`
  with no per-card override (confirmed by reading
  `snippets/collection-card.liquid` directly, not assumed from schema).
  Caption is optional per instance — the category rows pass `""` and
  render heading-only, matching their own source design.

  Not bound to a collection, deliberately, for all three rows now: the
  four occasions still aren't real Shopify collections (2026-08-21), and
  the three categories are real collections but their tile needs a href
  a collection-list card can't produce — so all three rows carry their
  heading as plain theme copy and their image via direct `image_picker`
  rather than `closest.collection.title`/`.image`. `link` has no
  default, and a card with no link set renders as a plain,
  non-interactive `<div>` instead of an `<a>` — not an `<a href="">`,
  which most browsers treat as a link to the current page and would
  still be clickable, just wrong. The homepage's four occasion cards were
  live with all four silently defaulting to /collections/all for a full
  session before anyone noticed, precisely because a working-looking
  fallback made an unconfigured card indistinguishable from a
  configured one (fixed 2026-08-24). An unconfigured card should be
  obviously unfinished — unclickable — not plausibly wrong.

  `alt` is passed as an explicit empty string on every instance
  (2026-09-14) — the card's own `heading` always renders as visible text
  in the same `<a>`, immediately under the image, so the image's meaning
  is already carried by adjacent text; a screen reader announcing the
  category name twice (once as alt, once as the heading) is worse than
  announcing it once. Briefly set to `block_settings.heading` earlier the
  same day, which was itself a fix for a real gap (this block emitted no
  alt at all, unlike the category tiles' previous native mechanism,
  which inherited alt from the bound collection) — corrected once the
  double-announcement was pointed out; see `REVIEW-NOTES.md`.

  Three settings make one block cover two visually distinct rows without
  a near-duplicate file: `image_ratio` (portrait 3:4, the occasion row's
  own original crop, vs square 1:1, the category row's original crop —
  the category source photos are landscape and lose real content at
  3:4), `scrim_depth` (tall, the occasion row's original 0/44/72% curve,
  vs compact, the category row's original 0/27/45% curve — see
  `design/DESIGN-TOKENS.md`'s scrim entry for why it was compressed) and
  `heading_style` (italic 26px, the occasion row's own type, vs upright
  30px, matching the category row's original `collection-title` block).
  Set per instance via inline CSS custom properties on the card's own
  root element, the same pattern Horizon's native blocks already use for
  per-instance values (`_collection-card`'s `--horizontal-alignment`,
  etc.) — avoids the fragility of a template- or section-id-scoped CSS
  override (the category row's original compact-scrim value lived in
  exactly that fragile shape, `[data-template="index"] .collection-card
  --image-bg .overlay { ... !important }` in `assets/lambruk-tokens.css`,
  now dead code and removed since nothing renders that markup anymore).
  That scoping is also why the Cafe page's own category tiles were never
  actually compressed to begin with — `[data-template="index"]` only
  ever matched the homepage, so Cafe's tiles carried the taller, darker
  curve the whole time despite otherwise identical settings to the
  homepage's. Both rows now use `compact` deliberately, restoring the
  homepage's intended look exactly and correcting Cafe's to match it,
  flagged rather than silently perpetuated.

  Sits inside a `group` block set to `content_direction: row` — this
  block's own outer div carries `flex: 1 1 0` so four cards share the row
  equally, the row-flex equivalent of the project's usual "block needs
  explicit width:100% to fill its container" rule (ARCHITECTURE.md /
  CLAUDE.md): a flex child left unsized just shrinks to its own content
  instead of sharing space evenly.

  `flex: 1 1 0` only applies from 750px up (Horizon's own mobile
  breakpoint, confirmed in assets/base.css). Below it, the wrapping
  group's own `vertical_on_mobile` setting switches the parent to
  `flex-direction: column` — at that point `flex-basis: 0` governs
  *height*, not width, and with the parent's own height set to hug its
  content (no fixed height to grow into), every card collapsed to
  `height: 0` in testing, confirmed live via getBoundingClientRect (not
  assumed from how flexbox is supposed to behave) — a real, reproduced
  bug, not a hypothetical one. Below 750px this block instead takes
  `width: 100%` and drops the flex sizing entirely, so height comes from
  its own `aspect-ratio` like a normal block.
{%- enddoc -%}

{% liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings

  case block_settings.image_ratio
    when 'square'
      assign card_aspect_ratio = '1 / 1'
    else
      assign card_aspect_ratio = '3 / 4'
  endcase

  case block_settings.scrim_depth
    when 'compact'
      assign scrim_mid_pct = '27%'
      assign scrim_top_pct = '45%'
    else
      assign scrim_mid_pct = '44%'
      assign scrim_top_pct = '72%'
  endcase

  case block_settings.heading_style
    when 'upright'
      assign heading_font_style = 'normal'
      assign heading_font_size = '30px'
    else
      assign heading_font_style = 'italic'
      assign heading_font_size = '26px'
  endcase

  assign card_style = '--occasion-card-ratio: ' | append: card_aspect_ratio | append: '; --occasion-card-scrim-mid: ' | append: scrim_mid_pct | append: '; --occasion-card-scrim-top: ' | append: scrim_top_pct | append: '; --occasion-card-heading-style: ' | append: heading_font_style | append: '; --occasion-card-heading-size: ' | append: heading_font_size | append: ';'
%}

{% capture card_body %}
  {%- if block_settings.image != blank -%}
    {{
      block_settings.image
      | image_url: width: 800
      | image_tag: widths: '400, 600, 800', sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 25vw, 50vw', class: 'lambruk-occasion-card__image', loading: 'lazy', alt: ''
    }}
  {%- endif -%}
  <div class="lambruk-occasion-card__scrim"></div>
  <div class="lambruk-occasion-card__text">
    {%- if block_settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h3 class="lambruk-occasion-card__heading">{{ block_settings.heading }}</h3>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if block_settings.caption != blank -%}
      <p class="lambruk-occasion-card__caption">{{ block_settings.caption }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{% endcapture %}

{%- if block_settings.link != blank -%}
  <a
    href="{{ block_settings.link }}"
    class="lambruk-occasion-card spacing-style"
    style="{{ card_style }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >{{ card_body }}</a>
{%- else -%}
  <div
    class="lambruk-occasion-card spacing-style"
    style="{{ card_style }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >{{ card_body }}</div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .lambruk-occasion-card {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: var(--occasion-card-ratio, 3 / 4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .lambruk-occasion-card {
      width: auto;
      flex: 1 1 0;
      min-width: 0;
    }
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-card__image {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-card__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(
      0deg,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.86) 0%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.46) var(--occasion-card-scrim-mid, 44%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) var(--occasion-card-scrim-top, 72%)
    );
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-card__text {
    position: absolute;
    left: 22px;
    right: 22px;
    bottom: 22px;
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-card__heading {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-style: var(--occasion-card-heading-style, italic);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--occasion-card-heading-size, 26px);
    color: #F7F5F2;
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-card__caption {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: rgba(247, 245, 242, 0.78);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.lambruk_occasion_card",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:settings.image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "t:settings.heading",
      "default": "Occasion"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "caption",
      "label": "t:settings.caption",
      "default": "Curated for the occasion."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "link",
      "label": "t:settings.link"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_ratio",
      "label": "t:settings.image_ratio",
      "options": [
        { "value": "portrait", "label": "t:options.portrait" },
        { "value": "square", "label": "t:options.square" }
      ],
      "default": "portrait"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "scrim_depth",
      "label": "t:settings.lambruk_occasion_card_scrim_depth",
      "options": [
        { "value": "tall", "label": "t:options.tall" },
        { "value": "compact", "label": "t:options.compact" }
      ],
      "default": "tall"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_style",
      "label": "t:settings.lambruk_occasion_card_heading_style",
      "options": [
        { "value": "italic", "label": "t:options.italic" },
        { "value": "upright", "label": "t:options.upright" }
      ],
      "default": "italic"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
